/target

# Wallet files, in case one is ever created inside the source tree while
# testing. Note this is a pattern, not a directory: `data/` holds packaging
# assets that must be tracked — icons, the desktop entry — and ignoring it
# silently kept them out of the repository.
*.sieve

# Source tarballs made while testing the PKGBUILD. `makepkg` builds one from
# the working tree and leaves it here; one was committed that way. The
# release workflow produces the real ones, and they belong on a release
# rather than in the history.
/*.tar.gz
/*.tar.xz
/pkg/
/src-pkg/

# What makepkg leaves behind when run in the source tree.
/packaging/aur/pkg/
/packaging/aur/src/
/packaging/aur/*.pkg.tar.zst
